asr-000260
00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:33.260
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: mga near poor ay talagang

asr-000261
00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sobrang mga nangangailangan pa rin

asr-000262
00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:38.300
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at marami ay walang sapat na kabuhayan,

asr-000263
00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: walang sapat na pinagkakakitaan.

asr-000264
00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya nga naman ay masasabi natin

asr-000265
00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.400
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na marami pa ring mga programa

asr-000266
00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:47.420
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ang kinakailangan

asr-000267
00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para matiyak na yung mga sinasabi

asr-000268
00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:50.460
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ng mga nakatawid

asr-000269
00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ay mananatiling makatawid.

asr-000270
00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:53.840
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya po,

asr-000271
00:09:53.840 --> 00:10:16.740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ano ba yung mga garantiya at mga programa na magtitiyak na yung mga kababayan natin na sinasabi natin na wala na doon sa poverty threshold, na sa tingin ho natin ay napakababa pa rin doon sa kasalukuyang mataas na presyo ng mga bilihin,

asr-000272
00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:26.260
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ay mananatili sila na may mas mataas na opportunities na magkaroon ng disenting sahod at trabaho.

asr-000273
00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:37.160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa katunayan din, Madam Speaker, noong pumarap din dito ang DOLE, sinabi rin natin sa kanila yung concern din ng isa nating kasamahan tungkol sa mababang sahod.

asr-000274
00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:46.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa na-report sa atin ng DepDev, sinabi nila na ang poverty threshold ngayon nasa 16,842 para sa pamilya ng lima sa NCR.

asr-000275
00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:56.560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At sa labas naman ito, nasa 14,634. Sa NCR pa lang, nasa 488 pesos lang po yan kada araw.

asr-000276
00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:03.740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngunit, kung sa NCR, medyo konting mas aangat yung minimum wage doon sa 488.

asr-000277
00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:13.520
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero kung sa labas po ng NCR, nasa labing dalawa na region yung minimum wage na mas mababa sa threshold ng DepDev.

asr-000278
00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At kumbaga, hindi talaga sapat na isa lang yung nagtatrabaho.

asr-000279
00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:26.900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kailangan pa maraming nagtatrabaho o may dagdag na pagkakakitaan yung mga miyembro ng isang household.

asr-000280
00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:41.520
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At makikita natin yan doon sa presentation din ng DepDev na pagamat meron tayong nasa 4 million jobs generated from 2020 to date,

asr-000281
00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:46.280
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: marami naman dito ay underemployed.

asr-000282
00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:54.220
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kumbaga, nagahanap pa ng dagdag na trabaho o kaya naman nadagdag doon sa kanilang current na pinagkakitaan

asr-000283
00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:58.140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: o kaya naman ay nagtatrabaho ng less than 40 hours per week.

asr-000284
00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:06.260
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ibig sabihin, talagang nagahanap ng dagdag, dagdag na kita bilang pangsuporta sa kanilang mga pamilya.

asr-000285
00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:10.260
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman po, meron tayong...

asr-000286
00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:23.540
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ito, napakalaki ng pondo natin para sa emergency assistance tulad ng TUPAD, ng AEC, ng MAEFIP para sa iba't ibang mga pangangailangan.

asr-000287
00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:33.240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero, konti lang yung pondo para doon sa mga programang pagpapanatili sa kanila doon sa labas ng poverty.

asr-000288
00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:40.540
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Halimbawa, yung Sustainable Livelihood Program, yung Micro-Small-Medium Enterprise Development Program.

asr-000289
00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:50.060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sobrang konti lang yan, konting turot doon sa buong nabanggit natin ng mga programa na nasa daang-daang bilyon na.

asr-000290
00:12:50.240 --> 00:13:00.900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya po, dito pa lang sa tingin ko, malaki na yung problema natin kung paano ba natin matitiyak na yung mga nakatawid ay hindi babalik doon sa lubos na kahirapan at gutom.

asr-000291
00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:10.520
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, nais ko pong magtanong tungkol sa mga public-private partnership projects na meron.

asr-000292
00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:20.540
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Halimbawa po, sa Naiya PPP Project, isa sa mga natagurian na fastest approved PPP proposal sa kasaysayan ng Pilipinas.

asr-000293
00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:29.920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pagkatapos ng six weeks na evaluation, ito po ay naaprobahan ng NEDA noon, ngayon po ay Dep-Dev Board na.

asr-000294
00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:38.880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang tanong ko, Madam Speaker, bago po ba ito maaprobahan, nagkaroon ba ng consultation sa mga affected stakeholders?

asr-000295
00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:46.240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ano ang naging mekanism ng consultation? Ilang stakeholder consultations ba ang naisagawa?

asr-000296
00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:53.500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sino-sino ang nakonsulta? At paano isinama sa concession agreement ang kanilang mga recommendations?

asr-000297
00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:10.520
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Madam Speaker, tumatakbo po yung oras ko kahit hinihintay pa po natin.

asr-000298
00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:12.220
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang ating distinct sponsor.

asr-000299
00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:15.780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000300
00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:29.500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, in terms of the creation of the feasibility study, that is where the consultations for all local stakeholders were relevant to that particular project.

asr-000301
00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:31.800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: That is where it's conducted.

asr-000302
00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So, for the record, nagkaroon po ng konsulta.

asr-000303
00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:45.080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, as for the Dep-Dev.

asr-000304
00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:57.540
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ilang stakeholder consultations po yung nangyari. At lahat po ba ng affected na mga sectors sa na-IA ay ating nakonsulta?

asr-000305
00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.120
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At naipasok po ba yung kanilang mga...

asr-000306
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:08.000
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: rekomendasyon sa naging outcome ng pag-aproba ng proyekto na ito.

asr-000307
00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:14.860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, the DepDev is currently pulling out all details regarding to the project.

asr-000308
00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:21.220
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, we will just wait and we will submit to our distinguished colleague.

asr-000309
00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:51.200
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000310
00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:56.060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Abangan po natin ang ulat at submission mula sa ating distinguished sponsor at sa DepDev.

asr-000311
00:15:56.740 --> 00:16:02.140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman po ay kaugnay ng lumalaganap na privatization at mollification ng mga palengke.

asr-000312
00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:12.160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nasa palisiya ba ng pamahalaan na maipaubaya sa malalaking retailers yung pagpapaunlad ng ating public markets ngayon sa buong bansa?

asr-000313
00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:21.200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

asr-000314
00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:28.640
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: But the particular circumstance of that, Madam Speaker, that would be under the purview of the local government unit.

asr-000315
00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:37.640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pagamat, anan dyan po ang responsibilidad ng local government units noong pagdating sa market administration,

asr-000316
00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:50.920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: anan dyan din naman yung role halimbawa ng PPP Center pagdating sa pagtitiyak ng mga requirements at ng mga proposals na ito, lalong-lalo na sa mga USPs.

asr-000317
00:16:51.200 --> 00:17:08.180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Para matiyak na ito po ay hindi lang sumusunod sa mga requirements pero tumutugon din sa interest ng publiko, yung mutual benefits po ng publiko pati po ng privado pagdating sa ganitong mga proyekto.

asr-000318
00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:21.180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At ang panawagan ng ating mga public markets, public and people partners, lalong-lalo na sa public markets na may mga vendors associations, retailers associations.

asr-000319
00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:30.840
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Talagang people-powered yung ating mga public markets at sila po ay handang-handa kumbaga tuminding para maisalba ang kanilang public markets.

asr-000320
00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:37.560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil nakita din natin, Madam Speaker, sa maraming lugar na may PPP ang kanilang mga merkado.

asr-000321
00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:46.400
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Lalong-lalo na pag malalaking retailers yung pumasok sa kanilang mga markets, namamatay talaga yung mga maliliit na mga manininda.

asr-000322
00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:51.040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, tungkol po sa monitoring ng PPP.

asr-000323
00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:59.500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron po ba kayong evaluation pagdating sa mga PPP projects?

asr-000324
00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:12.980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nakikita niyo po ba halimbawa sa case ng naiya privatization na kapag tumataas po yung fees sa airport o halimbawa po nung tayo ay humarap sa oil price shock,

asr-000325
00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:20.980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: lahat po ng ka-up airports nagkaroon ng pag-suspend ng mga increases sa kanilang mga passenger service charges.

asr-000326
00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:44.280
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pagdating naman sa rental fees ng vendors, marami pong mga PPPs na mga markets nakabatay na yung kanilang increases sa rental fees at iba't-ibang mga fees.

asr-000327
00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:49.500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hindi na po sa LGU pero nakabatay na kung sino private nila na partner.

asr-000328
00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron po bang monitoring?

asr-000329
00:18:51.200 --> 00:19:01.940
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hindi na po bang monitoring at evaluation ang PPP center pagdating sa ganitong mga kaso at meron ba tayong mechanism for redress of grievances in these instances?

asr-000330
00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:12.100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, it would depend on the project. It's a project by project. It's a case by case basis.

asr-000331
00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:19.020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It would depend on what the provisions are in the terms of contract of the project.

asr-000332
00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:21.020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: However, I was assured...

asr-000333
00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:34.460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: I was assured by the DEF-DEF that at least in terms of seeking redress just in case there are problems or challenges then there is a mechanism that...

asr-000334
00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:41.460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: There is a mechanism established where those who have grievances can report directly to the PPP center.

asr-000335
00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:50.540
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa ngayon po ba meron kayong mga kaso na hinahawakan tungkol dito na halimbawa ang isang partner LGU ay nais na pong putulin,

asr-000336
00:19:50.540 --> 00:20:04.460
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: kung baga wakasan na yung kanilang kontrata na napirmahan sa panahon na hindi po nasusunod yung mga dapat na basunod na nakasaalang-alang pa rin yung interest ng publiko.

asr-000337
00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:17.340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sabi nga natin, di ba, partnership, pagdating sa mutual interest, mutual benefits, at hindi po yung isa lang ang pinakanakikinabang habang nasasakripisyo yung interest ng publiko.

asr-000338
00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:19.640
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000339
00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:30.060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The PPP center has, it's handling cases where there are complaints with regards to privatization projects.

asr-000340
00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.620
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: We will just furnish you a copy because it's quite voluminous.

asr-000341
00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:48.120
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker, at nananawagan din po ang representative ito dahil sa mga narinig natin ng mga issues at binanggit din ng ating sponsor na may mga complaints sa ngayon na hinaharap ang PPP center.

asr-000342
00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:49.740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa tingin ko, panahon na rin.

asr-000343
00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:55.640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So, ma-repaso, ma-review ng kapulungan na ito ang ating PPP center.

asr-000344
00:20:55.640 --> 00:21:08.180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So, alam ko po, relatibong bago ito pero nung naipasan natin yung bago, di ba, marami din pong mga sumulpot na mga issues, mga concerns na nasa tungkulin natin na pakinggan at bigyan ng aksyon.

asr-000345
00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:13.160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yun lamang sa ngayon. Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker. Maraming salamat sa ating distinguished sponsor.

asr-000346
00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:14.760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Majority Leader.

asr-000348
00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:20.520
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Madam Speaker, may we call on the Honorable Rene Luis Co.

asr-000349
00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:24.320
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Representative Rene Luis Co of the Kabataan Party-list for her interpellation.

asr-000350
00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:29.920
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Rene Luis Co of the Kabataan Party-list is now recognized for her interpellation.

asr-000351
00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:36.860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker, and good evening to our distinguished sponsor at 10 p.m.

asr-000352
00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:46.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, my question is in relation to the Philippine Development Plan 2023 to 2028,

asr-000353
00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:49.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and we'd like to be enlightened as to...

asr-000354
00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:57.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: some parts of it and even updates given that the funding that we're discussing

asr-000355
00:21:57.700 --> 00:22:04.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: will be about the second to the last year for the implementation of the Philippine Development Plan.

asr-000356
00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:10.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, within the Philippine Development Plan 2023 to 2028, I quote,

asr-000357
00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:17.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: it is said that education policies have undermined better performing private schools

asr-000358
00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:19.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: as seen in the declining share...

asr-000359
00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:23.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in private school enrollment, end quote.

asr-000360
00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:27.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, what does this mean?

asr-000361
00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:33.820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is this saying na negative key performance indicator ang pagbaba ng enrollment sa private schools?

asr-000362
00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:43.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For reference, this is page 45 of the Philippine Development Plan.

asr-000363
00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:01.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, if my time po...

asr-000373
00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:50.520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, while the Department is pulling up the justifications behind it,

asr-000374
00:25:50.540 --> 00:25:54.620
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Really, in terms of the declining share of private school enrollment,

asr-000375
00:25:55.060 --> 00:25:59.100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it's really because this was crafted in 2022,

asr-000376
00:26:00.400 --> 00:26:07.060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and during the pandemic period, a lot of private schools closed down.

asr-000377
00:26:07.780 --> 00:26:09.520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, at least on that part.

asr-000379
00:27:03.500 --> 00:27:21.000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: With indulgence of our distinguished colleague, the Department is now pulling up the justification behind this statement. But rest assured, at least on the part of DepDev,

asr-000380
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:40.800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: this is not, it won't be an indicator of development. It is quite an [unclear] statement to make.

asr-000380-split-2
00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:49.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At least on the part of this representation, that's not really aligned also with what the Philippine Development Plan endeavors to do.

asr-000381
00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:52.900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: I agree, Madam Speaker.

asr-000383
00:27:52.900 --> 00:27:57.360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, under Article 14, Section 4 of the 1987 Constitution,

asr-000384
00:27:57.660 --> 00:28:04.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: it says that the state recognizes the complementary roles of public and private institutions in the education system

asr-000385
00:28:04.800 --> 00:28:10.300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and shall exercise reasonable supervision and regulation of all educational institutions.

asr-000386
00:28:11.220 --> 00:28:13.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We are alarmed by this statement, Madam Speaker,

asr-000387
00:28:13.960 --> 00:28:20.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: because EDCOM 2 has noted the trend in state universities and colleges,

asr-000388
00:28:20.540 --> 00:28:31.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: as well as even basic educational institutions of the increase in enrollment in public educational institutions,

asr-000389
00:28:31.860 --> 00:28:37.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: especially because of the advent of the universal access to quality tertiary education.

asr-000390
00:28:37.820 --> 00:28:44.380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, to see this statement is alarming because it is saying,

asr-000391
00:28:44.560 --> 00:28:47.540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and we're still continuously wondering what it's saying particularly,

asr-000392
00:28:47.540 --> 00:28:49.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: is it saying na,

asr-000393
00:28:50.540 --> 00:28:57.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: yung pagbaba ng kalidad ng administrasyon ay sanhi ng pagbaba ng enrollment sa private schools?

asr-000394
00:28:57.820 --> 00:29:00.860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Or is it saying na ang pagbaba ng enrollment sa private schools

asr-000395
00:29:00.860 --> 00:29:05.900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ay may implication din po ba ng pagbaba ng kalidad ng edukasyon?

asr-000396
00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:15.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And does that not violate the complementarity principle of private and public education institutions as provided by the Constitution?

asr-000397
00:29:15.060 --> 00:29:20.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, can the Department submit a written explanation?

asr-000398
00:29:20.540 --> 00:29:26.940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, can the Department submit a written explanation for this statement which is in the Philippine Development Plan?

asr-000399
00:29:26.940 --> 00:29:39.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And if it would like to roll back maybe on that statement so as to not violate the complementarity principle of public and private educational institutions?

asr-000400
00:29:40.180 --> 00:29:40.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker?

asr-000401
00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:44.380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, Honorable Co.

asr-000402
00:29:44.380 --> 00:29:50.200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, that will comply, particularly with the detailed justification of why this,

asr-000403
00:29:50.540 --> 00:29:53.360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ah, statement was put inside the Philippine Development Plan.

asr-000404
00:29:53.860 --> 00:29:54.120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes.

asr-000405
00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:56.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, just as a final note,

asr-000406
00:29:56.920 --> 00:29:59.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ah, it has not escaped this representation.

asr-000407
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:11.280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: attention that there has been an increase in policies wherein there is an intent to roll back

asr-000408
00:30:11.280 --> 00:30:19.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: support of the state to educational institutions, whether it be for pushing for public-private

asr-000409
00:30:19.720 --> 00:30:25.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: partnerships in the creation of classrooms or the pushing of public-private partnerships

asr-000410
00:30:25.700 --> 00:30:32.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in creating commercial spaces in higher educational institutions so as they could be

asr-000411
00:30:32.840 --> 00:30:41.080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: fiscally autonomous and thereby, at the end of the day, just provide justification for

asr-000412
00:30:41.080 --> 00:30:48.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: either cutting or lessening the budget to be allocated to them, which to this representation

asr-000413
00:30:48.180 --> 00:30:53.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: might be averse to the targets provided in the PDP itself.

asr-000414
00:30:54.640 --> 00:30:55.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Under this,

asr-000415
00:30:55.700 --> 00:31:04.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I think page 48, it also says that government spending on education will be increased to 4-6%

asr-000416
00:31:04.440 --> 00:31:13.740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: of GDP in line with the Education 2030 Framework for Action. So, unfortunately, it is also this

asr-000417
00:31:13.740 --> 00:31:14.300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: um

asr-000418
00:31:14.300 --> 00:31:25.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the provision of the NEP that the GDP to budget ratio to education has been,

asr-000419
00:31:25.700 --> 00:31:47.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: lessened to around 3.95%, so I'd like to ask, kamusta po ba yung paggamit natin ng target na po ito na 6% of the GDP sana yung naka-allot sa education, given that we only have 2 years left to meet the targets of PDP? Madam Speaker.

asr-000420
00:31:47.340 --> 00:31:50.340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, thank you Madam Speaker.

asr-000421
00:31:50.340 --> 00:31:55.340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Well, at least in the Philippine Development Plan,

asr-000422
00:31:55.700 --> 00:31:59.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: as has been the policy of the national government,

asr-000423
00:31:59.700 --> 00:32:02.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: education has to be a priority.

asr-000424
00:32:02.700 --> 00:32:04.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Unfortunately,

asr-000425
00:32:04.700 --> 00:32:09.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: DepDev's mandate is really just to formulate policies and recommend

asr-000426
00:32:09.700 --> 00:32:16.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: those policies, but it doesn't have power over the actual allocation of budget

asr-000427
00:32:16.700 --> 00:32:19.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: for the education sector.

asr-000428
00:32:19.700 --> 00:32:22.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May this representation ask, how has the department

asr-000429
00:32:22.700 --> 00:32:24.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: either

asr-000430
00:32:24.700 --> 00:32:27.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: formulated a plan

asr-000431
00:32:27.700 --> 00:32:29.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: or forwarded

asr-000432
00:32:29.700 --> 00:32:31.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the meeting of the target

asr-000433
00:32:31.700 --> 00:32:33.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that there ought to be 6%

asr-000434
00:32:33.700 --> 00:32:35.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: of the budget

asr-000435
00:32:35.700 --> 00:32:37.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: allocated, equivalent

asr-000436
00:32:37.700 --> 00:32:39.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to our GDP, allocated

asr-000437
00:32:39.700 --> 00:32:41.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to education? So,

asr-000438
00:32:41.700 --> 00:32:43.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: as we know, it could have went to classrooms,

asr-000439
00:32:43.700 --> 00:32:45.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: it could have went to feeding programs,

asr-000440
00:32:45.700 --> 00:32:47.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: it could have went to the many capital outlay

asr-000441
00:32:47.700 --> 00:32:49.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: requests of our

asr-000442
00:32:49.700 --> 00:32:51.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: state universities and colleges.

asr-000443
00:32:51.700 --> 00:32:53.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Unfortunately, what is

asr-000444
00:32:53.700 --> 00:32:54.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: still observable

asr-000445
00:32:54.700 --> 00:32:56.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: is that 49

asr-000446
00:32:56.700 --> 00:32:58.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: out of the 113

asr-000447
00:32:58.700 --> 00:33:00.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: state universities and colleges

asr-000448
00:33:00.700 --> 00:33:02.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: suffered

asr-000449
00:33:02.700 --> 00:33:04.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: a lowering

asr-000450
00:33:04.700 --> 00:33:06.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: of their budgets compared to last year,

asr-000451
00:33:06.700 --> 00:33:08.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: we call it a budget cut.

asr-000452
00:33:08.700 --> 00:33:10.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We also noticed the lowering,

asr-000453
00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:12.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: a historic high

asr-000454
00:33:12.700 --> 00:33:14.700
