00:43:20.700 --> 00:43:22.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is this the framework that

asr-000752
00:43:22.700 --> 00:43:24.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the United States is entering into

asr-000753
00:43:24.700 --> 00:43:26.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that different countries

asr-000754
00:43:26.700 --> 00:43:28.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: are also being involved in

asr-000755
00:43:28.700 --> 00:43:30.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at this rate? So

asr-000756
00:43:30.700 --> 00:43:32.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: any feedback from the Department

asr-000757
00:43:32.700 --> 00:43:34.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: would be greatly appreciated Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-000758
00:43:34.700 --> 00:43:36.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: That is all.

asr-000759
00:43:36.700 --> 00:43:38.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you Madam Speaker.

asr-000760
00:43:44.700 --> 00:43:46.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: That is all Madam Speaker.

asr-000761
00:43:46.700 --> 00:43:48.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I yield to the floor. Thank you.

asr-000762
00:43:48.700 --> 00:43:50.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Majority Leader,

asr-000763
00:43:50.700 --> 00:43:52.700
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Madam Speaker.

asr-000764
00:43:52.700 --> 00:43:54.700
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Madam Speaker, may we recognize

asr-000765
00:43:54.700 --> 00:43:56.700
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Representative Iris Marie

asr-000766
00:43:56.700 --> 00:43:58.700
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Demesa Montes of the 4K

asr-000767
00:43:58.700 --> 00:44:00.700
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Partylist for her interpolation.

asr-000768
00:44:00.700 --> 00:44:02.700
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Iris Marie

asr-000769
00:44:02.700 --> 00:44:04.700
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Demesa Montes of 4K Partylist

asr-000770
00:44:04.700 --> 00:44:06.700
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: is now recognized for her interpolation.

asr-000771
00:44:06.700 --> 00:44:08.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you Madam Speaker.

asr-000772
00:44:08.700 --> 00:44:10.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: My questions

asr-000773
00:44:10.700 --> 00:44:12.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: will, my first

asr-000774
00:44:12.700 --> 00:44:14.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: question is

asr-000775
00:44:14.700 --> 00:44:16.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: for the DBM.

asr-000776
00:44:16.700 --> 00:44:18.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: The proposed health

asr-000777
00:44:18.700 --> 00:44:20.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: allocation is lower

asr-000778
00:44:20.700 --> 00:44:22.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: than 95.7 billion

asr-000779
00:44:22.700 --> 00:44:24.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: despite continuing

asr-000780
00:44:24.700 --> 00:44:26.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: obligations under

asr-000781
00:44:26.700 --> 00:44:28.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: RA 11223.

asr-000782
00:44:28.700 --> 00:44:30.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: What explains this

asr-000783
00:44:30.700 --> 00:44:32.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: decline, what criteria guided

asr-000784
00:44:32.700 --> 00:44:34.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: it, and which programs and

asr-000785
00:44:34.700 --> 00:44:36.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: services were reduced?

asr-000799
00:45:23.000 --> 00:45:25.640
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000800
00:45:25.640 --> 00:45:27.480
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: A couple of factors.

asr-000801
00:45:27.480 --> 00:45:32.900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: One is the utilization of the HFEP, particularly in 2026.

asr-000802
00:45:33.780 --> 00:45:38.500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So for fiscal year 2027, we reverted back to NEP level.

asr-000803
00:45:40.080 --> 00:45:43.000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Second, there is a reduction to the MYFIP.

asr-000804
00:45:43.820 --> 00:45:45.200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Again, back to the NEP level.

asr-000805
00:45:46.000 --> 00:45:50.780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Also, there is the factor of the one-time return of the 60 billion of PhilHealth funds,

asr-000806
00:45:51.180 --> 00:45:54.800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: which we cannot be sustained for the coming year.

asr-000807
00:45:56.300 --> 00:45:56.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay.

asr-000808
00:45:56.900 --> 00:46:01.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: May I, can you please repeat the one about PhilHealth?

asr-000809
00:46:02.380 --> 00:46:04.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Which one cannot be sustained?

asr-000810
00:46:07.480 --> 00:46:11.340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Oh yes, this pertains to the Supreme Court decision, Madam Speaker.

asr-000811
00:46:11.820 --> 00:46:14.280
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So there is a one-time return of 60 billion.

asr-000812
00:46:15.120 --> 00:46:18.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay, thank you, thank you, good sponsor, Madam Speaker.

asr-000813
00:46:19.080 --> 00:46:25.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How much of the reduction represents genuine deficiency savings, if at all?

asr-000814
00:46:25.480 --> 00:46:26.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And how much?

asr-000815
00:46:26.900 --> 00:46:29.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: It simply means less government provision for health services.

asr-000816
00:46:45.820 --> 00:46:53.080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, really the reduction would not be about the efficiency rate.

asr-000817
00:46:53.200 --> 00:46:56.860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It's really about the low absorptive capacity and the delays.

asr-000818
00:46:56.980 --> 00:46:57.540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And the implementation.

asr-000819
00:46:59.040 --> 00:46:59.460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker.

asr-000820
00:47:00.240 --> 00:47:03.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

asr-000821
00:47:04.780 --> 00:47:11.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kapansin din po, bumaba ang alokasyon ng PhilHealth mula sa 129 billion ngayong taon

asr-000822
00:47:11.800 --> 00:47:18.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: tungo sa 74 billion para sa 2027 o bawas ng 55 billion.

asr-000823
00:47:19.740 --> 00:47:21.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Bakit po kaya ito binawasan?

asr-000824
00:47:22.240 --> 00:47:26.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Gayong dapat lumalawak ang binipisyo at mas mabilis natin na,

asr-000825
00:47:26.820 --> 00:47:30.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na aabot ang mga adhikain ng universal health care.

asr-000826
00:47:31.160 --> 00:47:41.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At kasama po ba doon sa 95.7 billion na binaba, itong 55 billion na binaba sa pondo ng PhilHealth?

asr-000827
00:47:42.580 --> 00:47:46.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000828
00:47:48.200 --> 00:47:50.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Well, pertaining to what we mentioned,

asr-000829
00:47:50.660 --> 00:47:56.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: there was a 60 billion one-time return for PhilHealth Funds.

asr-000830
00:47:56.820 --> 00:48:03.820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, if you're accounting for that, actually, the 129 billion actually was just 69 billion.

asr-000831
00:48:05.060 --> 00:48:09.720
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Actually, nadagdagan pa po by 5 billion for this year, PhilHealth.

asr-000832
00:48:10.900 --> 00:48:11.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay.

asr-000833
00:48:12.200 --> 00:48:15.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

asr-000834
00:48:15.820 --> 00:48:19.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Dahil ang UHC ay nakabatay po sa progressive realization,

asr-000835
00:48:21.280 --> 00:48:26.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: aling targets ang maaantala o hindi matutupad dahil sa nabawas na po,

asr-000836
00:48:26.820 --> 00:48:32.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa pondo lalo sa primary care, outpatient services at catastrophic services.

asr-000837
00:48:38.400 --> 00:48:40.300
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Actually, Madam Speaker,

asr-000838
00:48:41.500 --> 00:48:45.120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: pag nagdagdagan po, kasi kung natanggal po yung 60 billion,

asr-000839
00:48:46.420 --> 00:48:48.820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: actually, dagdagan pa po ng 5 billion. So, actually, wala po nabawas.

asr-000840
00:48:49.520 --> 00:48:53.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sige po. Kung atin pong igigiet and we follow that line of argument,

asr-000841
00:48:54.160 --> 00:48:56.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung 60 billion po kasing binalik,

asr-000842
00:48:56.820 --> 00:48:58.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: meron naman po talaga ng PhilHealth.

asr-000843
00:48:58.720 --> 00:49:02.660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ibig sabihin, kung yan po ang argumento natin,

asr-000844
00:49:03.040 --> 00:49:10.420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: at this level, hindi pa rin nagbabago ang ibinibigay nating pondo para sa PhilHealth.

asr-000845
00:49:10.420 --> 00:49:18.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, meaning, sa 65 billion dati na ibinigay at ngayon ay nagkakahalagan ng 74 billion

asr-000846
00:49:18.700 --> 00:49:23.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na kiniklaim po natin na nagdagdag pa ng 5 billion. Tama po?

asr-000847
00:49:24.940 --> 00:49:26.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ayon po sa Section 37.

asr-000848
00:49:26.820 --> 00:49:33.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang RA 11223, malinaw na anim ang pinagkukuhanan ng pondo ng PhilHealth.

asr-000849
00:49:34.600 --> 00:49:41.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nandiyan dyan po yung sin tax revenues, yung PAGCOR share, yung PCSO share,

asr-000850
00:49:41.460 --> 00:49:45.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung premium contributions, yung galing sa DOH appropriations,

asr-000851
00:49:46.700 --> 00:49:50.280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: at national government subsidy sa GAA.

asr-000852
00:49:50.720 --> 00:49:52.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, anim po na items.

asr-000853
00:49:52.560 --> 00:49:55.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Para sa 2027, magkano?

asr-000854
00:49:56.820 --> 00:50:01.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: 74 billion, paano po natin maibibreak down itong,

asr-000855
00:50:01.720 --> 00:50:04.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: except of course, the premium contributions of members.

asr-000856
00:50:05.460 --> 00:50:11.160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ano po ang mag-a-account sa 74 billion na ito?

asr-000857
00:50:11.260 --> 00:50:15.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How much is from the sin tax, from the PAGCOR, from the PCSO?

asr-000858
00:50:18.640 --> 00:50:21.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, what does the 74 billion po represent?

asr-000859
00:50:23.480 --> 00:50:24.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ito, ito, ito, ito, ito.

asr-000860
00:50:26.820 --> 00:50:32.240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000861
00:50:32.520 --> 00:50:35.580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 55 billion will come from national government subsidies.

asr-000862
00:50:36.760 --> 00:50:41.500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 19 billion will come from a share of income from PAGCOR and PCSO.

asr-000863
00:50:42.680 --> 00:50:44.140
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, that is the 74.

asr-000864
00:50:44.140 --> 00:50:46.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: 55 billion will come from?

asr-000865
00:50:46.600 --> 00:50:47.740
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: National government subsidy.

asr-000866
00:50:48.440 --> 00:50:50.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: National government. So, saan po yung sin tax?

asr-000867
00:50:50.380 --> 00:50:53.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Where is sin tax? Wala pong alokasyon dito ang sin tax?

asr-000868
00:50:56.820 --> 00:51:05.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Subsidy po ito, because this is the first time I'm hearing that the government is going to give a 55 billion subsidy to PhilHealth.

asr-000869
00:51:05.940 --> 00:51:12.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Because normally, in the past years, ang pinagagalingan po ng pondo ng PhilHealth ay sin tax lamang.

asr-000870
00:51:13.040 --> 00:51:16.240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker. A point of clarification from the DBM.

asr-000871
00:51:16.460 --> 00:51:18.980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It is, the 55 billion is coming from the sin tax.

asr-000872
00:51:19.140 --> 00:51:19.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sin tax.

asr-000873
00:51:19.920 --> 00:51:20.120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

asr-000874
00:51:20.120 --> 00:51:26.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, 55 billion sin tax, 19 billion from PCSO and PAGCOR.

asr-000875
00:51:26.820 --> 00:51:27.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: PAGCOR, is that correct?

asr-000876
00:51:27.840 --> 00:51:28.860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000877
00:51:29.380 --> 00:51:34.660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Itong 19 billion po ng PAGCOR, ano po ang nirepresent nito?

asr-000878
00:51:35.200 --> 00:51:50.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Siguro, tanungin ko na lamang po, simula noong 2022, magkano na po ang naibigay ng National Treasury sa PhilHealth mula sa share ng PAGCOR and PCSO?

asr-000879
00:51:51.040 --> 00:51:53.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi lumalabas po sa talaan.

asr-000880
00:51:55.100 --> 00:51:56.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Speaker.

asr-000881
00:51:56.820 --> 00:51:57.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I'm good sponsor.

asr-000882
00:51:57.580 --> 00:52:08.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Remember, last year, I took the floor and alam po ni Chair yun, nagkwenta po tayo kung magkano po ang utang ng gobyerno sa PhilHealth.

asr-000883
00:52:09.480 --> 00:52:19.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At lumabas po doon sa aming tala na mahigit 200 milyon ang pagkukulang ng gobyerno sa PhilHealth.

asr-000884
00:52:20.120 --> 00:52:26.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasama na po dyan yung mga arrears sa sin tax, PAGCOR and PCSO.

asr-000885
00:52:26.820 --> 00:52:36.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa talaan po ng PhilHealth ngayon, lumalabas na ang pagkukulang daw po, ang arrears daw po, ay 241 billion.

asr-000886
00:52:37.820 --> 00:52:47.980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Does DBM confirm the figure? Is that also your figure? That the arrears are more or less 241 billion?

asr-000887
00:52:56.820 --> 00:52:59.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000888
00:53:01.180 --> 00:53:08.600
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Well, the figure of the DBM is, the arrears would only be at 62 billion.

asr-000889
00:53:10.900 --> 00:53:13.820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 756,224,000.

asr-000890
00:53:14.720 --> 00:53:20.300
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, dito po ibabawas yung 19 billion from the share.

asr-000891
00:53:20.300 --> 00:53:26.400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I am surprised at the figure kasi last year nang nagkwentahan po kami sa floor,

asr-000892
00:53:26.820 --> 00:53:33.140
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: galing mismo po sa figure ng DOF and DBM, nasa 200 plus billion.

asr-000893
00:53:33.800 --> 00:53:39.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Wala naman pong naidadagdag na pondo ang DBM, bakit po 62 billion na lang ito?

asr-000894
00:53:40.880 --> 00:53:47.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nagbayad po ba or nagbigay po ba ng supplemental or additional funding ang DBM nang hindi nalalaman?

asr-000895
00:53:48.780 --> 00:53:53.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Para mabawasan ng ganito kalaking halaga yung arrears nila dapat, supposedly?

asr-000896
00:53:53.960 --> 00:53:58.200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000897
00:53:58.700 --> 00:54:04.420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The 62 billion in arrears are for the PAGCOR and PCSO.

asr-000898
00:54:05.560 --> 00:54:18.980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, for the sin taxes, the updated figure would be 143,878,444,000.

asr-000899
00:54:18.980 --> 00:54:23.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay. Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-000900
00:54:23.960 --> 00:54:30.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And can I just please request an official list from the DBM of the arrears

asr-000901
00:54:30.100 --> 00:54:37.400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and to be broken down sa mga specific items po na kailangan nilang ibigay.

asr-000902
00:54:37.840 --> 00:54:42.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yung arrears from the sin tax remittances, PAGCOR and PCSO share,

asr-000903
00:54:42.840 --> 00:54:53.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and in fact, meron dapat nga po silang babayaran na may legacy receivable po dapat ang PhilHealth sa kanila.

asr-000904
00:54:53.960 --> 00:54:58.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yung mga premium subsidy arrears from 2016 and prior.

asr-000905
00:54:58.180 --> 00:55:08.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But anyway, gusto ko lamang pong malaman talaga, i-reconcile yung figure kung magkano po talaga ang kakulangan ng DBM

asr-000906
00:55:08.920 --> 00:55:15.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: mula sa sin tax share, sa PAGCOR, sa PCSO, at yung kabuoang total po nito.

asr-000907
00:55:16.840 --> 00:55:20.480
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: We will submit, Madam Speaker.

asr-000908
00:55:20.640 --> 00:55:20.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes.

asr-000909
00:55:20.900 --> 00:55:23.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, it is established at alam naman po natin.

asr-000910
00:55:23.880 --> 00:55:29.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kaya lahat, hindi din po ipinagkakaila na may kakulangan po talaga, ano?

asr-000911
00:55:29.560 --> 00:55:33.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang gusto ko pong itanong na susunod, yung kakulangan na pondo po ito,

asr-000912
00:55:33.980 --> 00:55:39.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kasi may mga halimbawa po in the past, ang collection sa sin tax sabihin nyo po ay,

asr-000913
00:55:39.620 --> 00:55:44.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I'm not sure of the complete figure, but I would just like to establish that

asr-000914
00:55:44.380 --> 00:55:49.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung ibinibigay po ng DBM falls short sa tamang collection.

asr-000915
00:55:49.340 --> 00:55:50.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, kaya may arrears tayo.

asr-000916
00:55:50.840 --> 00:55:53.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ito po bang mga perang itong hindi na ibibigay?

asr-000917
00:55:54.040 --> 00:55:55.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nasaan na po ba ito?

asr-000918
00:55:55.860 --> 00:55:58.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nagamit na po ba ito o nasa general fund?

asr-000924
00:56:31.000 --> 00:56:33.880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000925
00:56:33.880 --> 00:56:40.880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: At least for the earmarked revenues, yes, these are earmarked for the UHC.

asr-000926
00:56:40.880 --> 00:56:50.500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: However, there isn't a mechanism in place where we can actually account for the cash that comes in for the earmarked revenue.

asr-000927
00:56:50.500 --> 00:56:51.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, sa batas,

asr-000928
00:56:52.520 --> 00:56:53.860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: earmarked revenue po talaga siya,

asr-000929
00:56:53.860 --> 00:56:56.540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: but it can be programmed later.

asr-000930
00:56:57.180 --> 00:56:59.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay, I'll pursue that

asr-000931
00:56:59.520 --> 00:57:01.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: a little bit later, good sponsor,

asr-000932
00:57:01.580 --> 00:57:02.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Chair, no?

asr-000933
00:57:03.220 --> 00:57:04.420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi ang gusto ko lang

asr-000934
00:57:04.420 --> 00:57:05.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: pong puntuhin diyan,

asr-000935
00:57:06.560 --> 00:57:08.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: DBM na rin po nagsabi na

asr-000936
00:57:08.560 --> 00:57:10.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: earmarked nga po yan.

asr-000937
00:57:10.560 --> 00:57:12.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At yung linaw po ba ng

asr-000938
00:57:12.560 --> 00:57:14.400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: desisyon ng Korte Suprema

asr-000939
00:57:14.400 --> 00:57:16.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: nung ibinalik, pinababalik

asr-000940
00:57:16.560 --> 00:57:18.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung 60 billion, hindi pa

asr-000941
00:57:18.580 --> 00:57:20.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: rin po ba yun ganun talinaw

asr-000942
00:57:20.640 --> 00:57:22.120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na ang sinasabi

asr-000943
00:57:22.120 --> 00:57:24.140
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na kung earmarked yan for

asr-000944
00:57:24.140 --> 00:57:26.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: this purpose, dapat doon

asr-000945
00:57:26.560 --> 00:57:28.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: lamang po siya gamitin.

asr-000946
00:57:33.860 --> 00:57:34.500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

asr-000947
00:57:34.820 --> 00:57:35.940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Well, under law,

asr-000948
00:57:36.240 --> 00:57:38.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: if it's earmarked for that particular purpose

asr-000949
00:57:38.700 --> 00:57:40.100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: then it should go

asr-000950
00:57:40.100 --> 00:57:42.380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: to that particular purpose, which is reinforced

asr-000951
00:57:42.380 --> 00:57:43.440
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: by the Supreme Court.

asr-000952
00:57:43.760 --> 00:57:46.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Going along that line, good sponsor,

asr-000953
00:57:47.460 --> 00:57:48.200
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kasi nga po,

asr-000954
00:57:48.400 --> 00:57:49.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: hindi na ibigay yung

asr-000955
00:57:49.900 --> 00:57:52.160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: koleksyon halimbawa ng sin tax.

asr-000956
00:57:52.540 --> 00:57:54.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kulang. Saan po

asr-000957
00:57:54.220 --> 00:57:56.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yun napunta? Kasi dapat earmarked

asr-000958
00:57:56.460 --> 00:57:58.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yun, sabi rin ng Supreme Court,

asr-000959
00:57:58.800 --> 00:58:00.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: dapat sa PhilHealth lang yun

asr-000960
00:58:00.460 --> 00:58:02.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kasi para sa UHC yun.

asr-000961
00:58:02.560 --> 00:58:03.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So asan na po yun?

asr-000962
00:58:04.160 --> 00:58:06.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yun po ang gusto ko po saanang malaman.

asr-000963
00:58:07.620 --> 00:58:08.660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Bakit po tayo

asr-000964
00:58:08.660 --> 00:58:10.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: nagkakaroon ng malaking kakulangan

asr-000965
00:58:10.740 --> 00:58:12.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: o pagkakautang

asr-000966
00:58:12.240 --> 00:58:14.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa PhilHealth kung sinusunod

asr-000967
00:58:14.180 --> 00:58:16.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: natin ang batas

asr-000968
00:58:16.180 --> 00:58:17.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na dapat napupunta yun

asr-000969
00:58:17.920 --> 00:58:18.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa PhilHealth?

asr-000970
00:58:21.420 --> 00:58:22.460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker,

asr-000971
00:58:23.400 --> 00:58:24.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: as per the

asr-000972
00:58:24.400 --> 00:58:26.440
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: DBM, the variance

asr-000973
00:58:26.440 --> 00:58:27.580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: would fall

asr-000974
00:58:27.580 --> 00:58:29.320
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: in the general fund.

asr-000975
00:58:30.040 --> 00:58:32.500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So it's still in the general fund

asr-000976
00:58:32.500 --> 00:58:34.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: as of now, as we

asr-000977
00:58:34.400 --> 00:58:36.360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: speak, it's in the general

asr-000978
00:58:36.360 --> 00:58:36.820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: fund.

asr-000979
00:58:40.060 --> 00:58:41.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes, Madam Speaker. Thank you.

asr-000980
00:58:42.240 --> 00:58:43.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Sponsor,

asr-000981
00:58:44.420 --> 00:58:45.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Speaker,

asr-000982
00:58:47.020 --> 00:58:50.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kung wala na pong

asr-000983
00:58:50.360 --> 00:58:52.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sapat na subsidy, yung

asr-000984
00:58:52.180 --> 00:58:54.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: binabanggit ko po sa inyo kanina

asr-000985
00:58:54.500 --> 00:58:56.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na anim na income streams

asr-000986
00:58:56.460 --> 00:58:57.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: dapat ng PhilHealth.

asr-000987
00:58:58.340 --> 00:58:59.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Supposedly po,

asr-000988
00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:02.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: meron pa doon government subsidy

asr-000989
00:59:02.360 --> 00:59:04.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: to represent, sana yan,

asr-000990
00:59:04.360 --> 00:59:06.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: subsidian ng gobyerno

asr-000991
00:59:06.080 --> 00:59:07.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: para sa mga indigent

asr-000992
00:59:07.920 --> 00:59:10.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: at saka para doon

asr-000993
00:59:10.320 --> 00:59:11.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa mga special laws.

asr-000994
00:59:12.240 --> 00:59:14.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Wala din pong naibibigay

asr-000995
00:59:14.460 --> 00:59:16.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: dyan ang gobyerno.

asr-000996
00:59:16.580 --> 00:59:18.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, kung susumahin po

asr-000997
00:59:18.440 --> 00:59:18.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: natin,

asr-000998
00:59:20.380 --> 00:59:22.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kulang na po ang naibibigay

asr-000999
00:59:22.360 --> 00:59:24.200
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: galing sa sin tax na

asr-001000
00:59:24.200 --> 00:59:24.980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: earmark,

asr-001001
00:59:26.080 --> 00:59:28.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: specifically, nakalagay

asr-001002
00:59:28.260 --> 00:59:29.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa UHC law,

asr-001003
00:59:30.280 --> 00:59:32.280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: hindi rin po naibibigay ng

asr-001004
00:59:32.280 --> 00:59:34.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: buo yung pag-core,

asr-001005
00:59:34.860 --> 00:59:35.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang PCSO,

asr-001006
00:59:36.120 --> 00:59:37.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: hindi rin po naibibigay,

asr-001007
00:59:38.480 --> 00:59:40.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: wala din pong subsidia

asr-001008
00:59:40.380 --> 00:59:42.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na galing sa gobyerno,

asr-001009
00:59:42.220 --> 00:59:44.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: for indigents and under special laws.

asr-001010
00:59:45.580 --> 00:59:45.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So,

asr-001011
00:59:46.360 --> 00:59:48.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: paano po natin, Madam Sponsor,

asr-001012
00:59:49.020 --> 00:59:49.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Speaker,

asr-001013
00:59:49.940 --> 00:59:52.420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: mapuprotektahan ang mga direct

asr-001014
00:59:52.420 --> 00:59:54.400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: contributors who bear

asr-001015
00:59:54.400 --> 00:59:56.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: the burden ng gastusin

asr-001016
00:59:56.940 --> 00:59:57.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ng PhilHealth?

asr-001017
00:59:58.500 --> 00:59:59.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mga ordinaryong

asr-001018
00:59:59.700 --> 01:00:03.300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: manggagawa po ito

asr-001019
01:00:03.300 --> 01:00:16.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na pilit na nagbabayad ng tama at sa takdang panahon. So pagdating ng punto na magkakasakit sila, kulang ang kanilang benepisyong nakukuha.

asr-001020
01:00:16.360 --> 01:00:32.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So paano po natin ito na justify at paano po natin na ipapaliwanag, maipapaliwanag ng DBM and our economic managers sa tuwing-tuwing nagbibigay po tayo ng pondo para sa universal healthcare.

asr-001022
01:01:16.360 --> 01:01:33.100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you Madam Speaker. Well, this representation shares the same sentiment as the Honorable Montez. As of now, there is really just a pool of social insurances.

asr-001023
01:01:33.100 --> 01:01:43.160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So there isn't a differentiation as of now, the way it's treated, the fund, in terms of direct and indirect contributors.

asr-001024
01:01:43.160 --> 01:01:46.340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So for the purposes of this,

asr-001025
01:01:46.360 --> 01:01:58.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the use of, and the programs of the PhilHealth, I think that would be better answered during the plenary deliberations of the Department of Health and the PhilHealth.

asr-001026
01:02:00.180 --> 01:02:05.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yeah, but I understand Madam Sponsor, but this is about financing.

asr-001027
01:02:06.140 --> 01:02:13.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So this is about financing, which is the responsibility of the DBM and our economic managers.

asr-001028
01:02:13.560 --> 01:02:15.660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: It's about prioritization.

asr-001029
01:02:15.660 --> 01:02:24.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: It's about our, it's about honoring our commitment to the promise of universal healthcare.

asr-001030
01:02:25.200 --> 01:02:37.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Well, anyway, ang gusto ko lamang pong ipunto na itong usaping ito ay hindi usapin ng fiscal space or absorptive capacity or programming decision lamang.

asr-001031
01:02:37.640 --> 01:02:42.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito ay usapin ng pagsunod sa batas at sa pangako ng gobyerno sa UHC.

asr-001032
01:02:43.260 --> 01:02:45.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Paano matutupad ang UHC?

asr-001033
01:02:45.660 --> 01:02:49.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung ang mismong lifeline ng PhilHealth ay napipigil.

asr-001034
01:02:50.640 --> 01:02:56.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: When government appropriations for PhilHealth are withheld and arrears rich billions of pesos,

asr-001035
01:02:56.680 --> 01:03:00.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: the state itself becomes a source of delayed financing.

asr-001036
01:03:01.080 --> 01:03:09.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung inaasa natin na magbabayad ang mga direct contributors, ang mga miyembro, sa tamang oras at tamang halaga,

asr-001037
01:03:10.540 --> 01:03:13.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: government should lead by example.

asr-001038
01:03:13.040 --> 01:03:21.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Dapat manguna ang gobyerno, ang pamahalaan, sa maagap at buong pagpupondo ng universal healthcare.

asr-001039
01:03:22.920 --> 01:03:26.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kaugnay po dito, Madam Speaker, Madam Sponsor,

asr-001040
01:03:26.040 --> 01:03:43.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: On August 4, 2006, the Philippines contracted an ADB-JICA policy loan of almost $938 million or roughly $60 billion for Build Universal Healthcare Subprogram 3.

asr-001041
01:03:43.040 --> 01:03:48.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Meron 3 na po ito, so ibig sabihin may 1 and 2.

asr-001042
01:03:49.200 --> 01:03:55.940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tanong ko po sa DBM and siguro sa economic managers natin, bakit kailangan mag-utang?

asr-001043
01:03:56.760 --> 01:04:02.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano ang terms? At saan eksaktong ginamit yung mga proceeds?

asr-001044
01:04:02.460 --> 01:04:05.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At saan po gagamitin itong sa Subprogram 3?

asr-001045
01:04:05.880 --> 01:04:12.880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, the loan?

asr-001046
01:04:13.040 --> 01:04:17.260
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mentioned by the Honorable Montez is a policy loan, so it's for budgetary support.

asr-001047
01:04:18.660 --> 01:04:20.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Budgetary support for?

asr-001048
01:04:22.560 --> 01:04:26.240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Or it finances the general fund. It goes to the general fund.

asr-001049
01:04:26.920 --> 01:04:33.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: To the general fund, but it has its use. Since it's a policy loan, alam ko pong may mga terms yun,

asr-001050
01:04:33.180 --> 01:04:39.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang maaari ko po bang malaman kahit ito na lang sa Subprogram 3, saan po yun gagamitin?

asr-001051
01:04:39.960 --> 01:04:42.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi ang ginamit po, universal healthcare.

asr-001052
01:04:43.040 --> 01:04:48.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So meaning, gagamitin po yan sa implementasyon ng universal healthcare.

asr-001053
01:05:12.360 --> 01:05:12.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay.

asr-001054
01:05:12.960 --> 01:05:27.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ayon po sa aking pananaliksik, ang sabihin ko na lamang po na yung package 3 daw po focuses on institutionalizing reforms to ensure long-term sustainability and system-wide integration,

asr-001055
01:05:27.800 --> 01:05:35.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: e-health infrastructure, automated claims processing, and resilient health system financing.

asr-001056
01:05:36.720 --> 01:05:40.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So ito pong mga ito ay dapat napupunta sa PhilHealth.

asr-001057
01:05:40.960 --> 01:05:51.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So ang tanong ko po, doon sa quinenta po natin, nagbigay po ba tayo galing sa loan na ito?

asr-001058
01:05:51.100 --> 01:06:00.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi ang mga quinenta po nating nakaraan galing lang sa arrears ng sin tax, wala pa nga pong kasama ang PAGCOR at PCSO.

asr-001059
01:06:00.820 --> 01:06:07.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ngayon po pala, meron ding policy loan. So saan napunta po yung policy loan?

asr-001060
01:06:10.960 --> 01:06:20.960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-001061
01:06:20.960 --> 01:06:32.220
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: As for the DBM, this particular policy loan goes to the general fund. So it's part of the general fund to fulfill the general fund requirements.

asr-001062
01:06:32.360 --> 01:06:39.980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: However, based on practice and the commitment of the national government is that this particular policy loan, so the proceeds from there,

asr-001063
01:06:40.960 --> 01:06:46.600
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: would be attributed to programs, activities, and projects of the DOH.

asr-001064
01:06:48.400 --> 01:06:51.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Madam Sponsor. Kaya lang naguluhan lang po ako.

asr-001065
01:06:51.600 --> 01:07:05.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Is it a normal practice that you contract a policy loan for, say, for the universal healthcare, pero hindi din mapupunta kung saan yung dapat mo purpose na inutang yun?

asr-001066
01:07:05.220 --> 01:07:08.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Is that what you're telling me, Madam Sponsor?

asr-001069
01:07:37.000 --> 01:07:40.960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, so

asr-001082
01:07:40.960 --> 01:07:47.420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: This policy loan is attributed to programs under the UHC, so not particularly just PhilHealth.

asr-001083
01:07:47.920 --> 01:07:54.260
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So as for the DBM, these would also include the HFEP and the MYFEP.

asr-001084
01:07:56.800 --> 01:08:05.020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So also, as for the DBM, we also have different policy loans for education, disaster management,

asr-001085
01:08:05.020 --> 01:08:10.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and usually the practice is that, so the loan proceeds goes to the general fund,

asr-001086
01:08:10.400 --> 01:08:17.820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: but there's a commitment on the part of the national government that the proceeds from that loan will go to,

asr-001087
01:08:18.200 --> 01:08:23.160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: for example, if it's education, it would be under the different agencies under the education sector,

asr-001088
01:08:23.840 --> 01:08:29.060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: or disaster management, it would go to specific PAPs.

asr-001089
01:08:29.440 --> 01:08:31.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: As for the DBM, Madam Speaker.

asr-001090
01:08:31.780 --> 01:08:35.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you. Good sponsor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001091
01:08:35.260 --> 01:08:40.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: May I just request, perhaps may I just request the DBM to submit to this representative?

asr-001092
01:08:40.400 --> 01:08:45.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Before the budget deliberations are done and over with,

asr-001093
01:08:45.560 --> 01:08:57.500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: details of the UHC loan for sub-programs 1, 2, 3.

asr-001094
01:08:57.760 --> 01:09:04.160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: For sub-programs 1 and 2, this representation would like to find out how much was borrowed,

asr-001095
01:09:04.160 --> 01:09:10.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: for what purpose, under what repayment terms, and which agencies were responsible,

asr-001096
01:09:10.400 --> 01:09:11.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: for implementation.

asr-001097
01:09:12.120 --> 01:09:15.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: That's for sub-programs 1 and 2.

asr-001098
01:09:16.540 --> 01:09:21.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And I would also like to find out, when are these loans due,

asr-001099
01:09:21.660 --> 01:09:27.400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and what is the projected fiscal burden on future budgets.

asr-001100
01:09:28.000 --> 01:09:35.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Perhaps it should be with the OF, but if the DBM can already give us the figure,

asr-001101
01:09:35.760 --> 01:09:37.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: we will highly appreciate that.

asr-001102
01:09:38.520 --> 01:09:40.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And more importantly, Madam Speaker,

asr-001103
01:09:40.400 --> 01:09:49.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I would like to request the DBM to submit the targets of sub-programs 1 and 2,

asr-001104
01:09:49.080 --> 01:09:54.220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and an assessment if, indeed, the targets have been achieved.

asr-001105
01:09:54.220 --> 01:10:00.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ang nakalagay po kasi doon na pinaggamitan ay gender-sensitive,

asr-001106
01:10:00.880 --> 01:10:08.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: climate-smart, and disaster-resilient improved coordination among public and private healthcare providers,

asr-001107
01:10:08.520 --> 01:10:09.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: increased number of sub-programs.

asr-001108
01:10:09.720 --> 01:10:14.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Number of primary care providers, enhanced health promotion services,

asr-001109
01:10:15.160 --> 01:10:21.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: increased health worker supply, and integrated delivery of quality health services.

asr-001110
01:10:22.300 --> 01:10:28.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito po bang mga to na mga targets ay na-achieve,

asr-001111
01:10:28.380 --> 01:10:34.280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kung hindi man, ilang porsyento na po tayo sa pag-achieve ng targets na yan

asr-001112
01:10:34.280 --> 01:10:38.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: nung pinasok ng ating gobyerno ang mga loans na ito.

asr-001113
01:10:39.420 --> 01:10:39.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam.

asr-001114
01:10:39.720 --> 01:10:46.480
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, the DBM will comply, particularly with the line-by-line details of sub-programs 1, 2,

asr-001115
01:10:46.600 --> 01:10:48.460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and the projections for sub-programs 2.

asr-001116
01:10:48.600 --> 01:10:52.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you so much, good sponsor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001117
01:10:53.040 --> 01:10:55.940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: In the end, gusto ko lang po sigurong sabihin,

asr-001118
01:10:55.940 --> 01:11:01.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: mahirap po kasing parang tanggapin na habang binabawasan natin

asr-001119
01:11:01.620 --> 01:11:04.940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: or hindi natin nabibigyan ng sapat na alokasyon,

asr-001120
01:11:05.940 --> 01:11:08.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang pagtupad ng universal healthcare,

asr-001121
01:11:09.720 --> 01:11:15.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ngutang pa rin po pala tayo na ginagamit ang universal healthcare,

asr-001122
01:11:15.600 --> 01:11:20.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: samantalang hindi naman natin nararamdaman yung inutang na iyon.

asr-001123
01:11:20.620 --> 01:11:26.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Dapat po, kung mangungutang tayo kasabay ng pondong binibigay ng gobyerno,

asr-001124
01:11:26.000 --> 01:11:31.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: dapat po parehong maghatid yan ng mas malawa, mas mabilis,

asr-001125
01:11:32.100 --> 01:11:35.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: at mas abot kayang serbisyong pangkalusugan.

asr-001126
01:11:35.960 --> 01:11:37.300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi naman po masama.

asr-001127
01:11:37.760 --> 01:11:38.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi pong masamang.

asr-001128
01:11:38.920 --> 01:11:39.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mangungutang tayo.

asr-001129
01:11:39.600 --> 01:11:45.980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mangungutang tayo para mas madali po nating maiabot yung pangako ng universal healthcare.

asr-001130
01:11:46.320 --> 01:11:50.280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pero sana po sa pag-utang na iyon, katulad din ng ibang utang,

asr-001131
01:11:50.640 --> 01:11:55.940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: nagagamit po talaga natin sa tamang paraan at kung saan po talaga natin,

asr-001132
01:11:56.580 --> 01:11:59.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: at kung para saan po talaga yung inutang natin.

asr-001133
01:11:59.960 --> 01:12:07.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At meron tayong targets at i-evaluate po natin yan kung natutupad yung mga targets na iyon.

asr-001134
01:12:07.520 --> 01:12:09.400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At at the end of the period,

asr-001135
01:12:09.600 --> 01:12:11.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: naubos na po natin ng pera,

asr-001136
01:12:11.700 --> 01:12:16.160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: masasabi natin yung inutang natin ay kapakipakinaban.

asr-001137
01:12:16.460 --> 01:12:25.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, let me just state again that the Supreme Court reminded us that where health begins, all freedoms stand.

asr-001138
01:12:25.860 --> 01:12:37.140
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung saan daw po nakatayo at nagsisimula ang kalusugan, doon nakatindig ang lahat ng kalayaan.

asr-001139
01:12:37.680 --> 01:12:39.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sana po isa puso natin.

asr-001140
01:12:39.600 --> 01:12:44.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito, bawat pagbalangkas natin ng budget para sa kalusugan.

asr-001141
01:12:45.100 --> 01:12:50.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kaya naman po, ang kababaihan, kabalikatan para sa katakanan at kaunlaran ng bayan or 4K,

asr-001142
01:12:51.200 --> 01:12:57.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ay maninindigan at patuloy na igigiip na ang universal healthcare ay hindi lamang pangako ng batas,

asr-001143
01:12:58.300 --> 01:13:00.540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kundi pananagutan ng gobyerno.

asr-001144
01:13:00.880 --> 01:13:07.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kung kulang ang pondo para sa UHC, kulang din ang hustisya at kalayaan ng bawat Pilipino.

asr-001145
01:13:07.320 --> 01:13:08.940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po.

asr-001146
01:13:09.600 --> 01:13:12.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Madam Speaker, Madam Sponsor, good evening po sa lahat.

asr-001147
01:13:12.740 --> 01:13:13.420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Authority Leader.

asr-001148
01:13:18.120 --> 01:13:28.280
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Dada Ismula from Akbayan Party List to interpolate on the proposed budget.

asr-001149
01:13:29.300 --> 01:13:32.640
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Dada Ismula is now recognized for her interpolation.

asr-001150
01:13:32.640 --> 01:13:38.080
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: As-salamu alaykum wa rahmatullah wa barakatuhu.

asr-001151
01:13:38.080 --> 01:13:39.160
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Madam Speaker, Madam Sponsor.

asr-001157
01:13:39.600 --> 01:14:00.120
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I want to focus on how the DBM ensures that syntax revenues are properly earmarked and transparently allocated para masigurong bawat Pilipino ay may libre o abot kaya at dekalidad na health services bilang karapatan natin.

asr-001158
01:14:00.120 --> 01:14:10.120
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: This is in continuation or in connection of what my colleague, Representative Iris Montes, have questioned earlier.

asr-001159
01:14:11.920 --> 01:14:27.560
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Madam Sponsor, can DBM confirm that under Republic Act No. 11223 or the Universal Health Care Act, health funding is statutory and non-discretionary?

asr-001160
01:14:27.560 --> 01:14:29.560
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ibig sabihin, nakasaad.

asr-001161
01:14:30.120 --> 01:14:36.760
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ibig sabihin, nasa batas at hindi basta babawasan, ihinto o ibahin ang paggagamitan.

asr-001162
01:14:38.500 --> 01:14:39.820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, we confirm, Madam Speaker.

asr-001163
01:14:40.520 --> 01:14:54.020
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Can DBM confirm that Republic Act No. 11346 and 11467 require specific percentages of all syntaxes to go directly to health programs?

asr-001164
01:14:54.820 --> 01:14:56.080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, we confirm.

asr-001165
01:14:56.080 --> 01:14:59.080
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Under Republic Act 11467.

asr-001166
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:12.660
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Can DBM confirm that 60% of excise taxes from alcohol, heated tobacco, and vapor products must go strictly to universal health care?

asr-001167
01:15:13.660 --> 01:15:14.420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-001168
01:15:14.420 --> 01:15:29.420
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Can DBM also confirm that under the same law, another 20% from these same taxes is legally reserved for medical assistance for indigent patients and for upgrading public hospitals?

asr-001169
01:15:30.760 --> 01:15:31.600
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-001170
01:15:32.400 --> 01:15:39.060
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Can DBM confirm that these health funds should be automatically appropriated by law?

asr-001171
01:15:39.060 --> 01:15:46.060
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ibig sabihin, hindi pwede bawasan o i-divert ng Pangulo o ng sino man sa Executive?

asr-001172
01:15:48.860 --> 01:15:58.200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, under RA11, under the Universal Health Care Act,

asr-001173
01:15:59.520 --> 01:15:59.980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: there is a...

asr-001174
01:15:59.980 --> 01:16:02.480
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It's supposed to be earmarked.

asr-001175
01:16:02.560 --> 01:16:04.160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: There is no...

asr-001176
01:16:04.160 --> 01:16:05.020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It's not automatic.

asr-001177
01:16:06.820 --> 01:16:10.080
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: But it is stated and appropriated by the law.

asr-001178
01:16:10.080 --> 01:16:15.560
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ibig sabihin, hindi po siya pwedeng i-divert ng Pangulo o ng sino man Executive?

asr-001179
01:16:16.760 --> 01:16:18.060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-001180
01:16:19.020 --> 01:16:21.900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker, Madam Sponsor.

asr-001181
01:16:22.440 --> 01:16:29.920
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Based on the DBM's budget document, or the Budget of Expenditures and Sources of Financing, or BESF,

asr-001182
01:16:29.980 --> 01:16:46.960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Table C.3, can DBM confirm that for 2026 projected tax collection from sweetened drinks reaches, or umaabot hanggang, P142.8 billion?

asr-001183
01:16:48.580 --> 01:16:50.120
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Again, projected po.

asr-001193
01:17:29.020 --> 01:17:37.160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, as for the BSF, that figure is correct, Madam Speaker.

asr-001194
01:17:37.160 --> 01:17:45.500
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat po. How about from alcohol? Tama po ba 153.6 billion pesos?

asr-001195
01:17:45.500 --> 01:18:07.680
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: For alcohol products, for Selective Exercise Tax on Goods, for 2027, the projection actually is 136.713 billion.

asr-001196
01:18:08.500 --> 01:18:12.740
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: This is under BESF po of Table C.3.

asr-001197
01:18:13.860 --> 01:18:14.660
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Okay.

asr-001198
01:18:14.940 --> 01:18:15.120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

asr-001199
01:18:15.120 --> 01:18:19.360
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And from tobacco po, 234.7 billion.

asr-001200
01:18:21.680 --> 01:18:31.620
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, at least as for the BESF Table C.3, for 2027, for tobacco, the projection would be 182.

asr-001201
